+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exited 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is it a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Fail fast: report the service is down" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast: report the failed POST" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast: fix the request" [shape=box];
+    "Retry up to 3 times (1 s, 2 s, 4 s; honor Retry-After)" [shape=box];
+    "Done" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exited 0?";
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Fail fast: report the service is down" [label="no"];
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Is it a POST?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST?" -> "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST?" -> "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [label="no"];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no, even on a timeout or 503"];
+    "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast: report the failed POST";
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [label="yes: retry with the same key"];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Fail fast: fix the request" [label="yes"];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Retry up to 3 times (1 s, 2 s, 4 s; honor Retry-After)" [label="no"];
+    "Fail fast: report the service is down" -> "Done";
+    "Fail fast: report the failed POST" -> "Done";
+    "Fail fast: fix the request" -> "Done";
+    "Retry up to 3 times (1 s, 2 s, 4 s; honor Retry-After)" -> "Done";
+}
+```
+
+A timeout does not mean the server never got the request: it may have created the order before the
+connection dropped. A 503 on a POST with no key is still a fail-fast, whatever the table row says.
+
